# PlatformIO device build output
.pio/

# Compiled host test binaries (built by test/Makefile; sources are kept)
test/test_*
!test/test_*.cpp
!test/test_*.h
!test/test_*.sh
# Built fuzz binaries (fuzz_obd, fuzz_obd_harness). Glob + negation so a new
# harness binary is covered automatically, matching the test/test_* rule above.
test/fuzz_obd*
!test/fuzz_obd*.cpp

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# UI snapshot renders are regenerated by tools/ui_snapshot (make snapshot)
tools/ui_snapshot/*.ppm
tools/ui_snapshot/*.png


# --- Secrets & PII (never commit) ---
# Private keys / credentials
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.env
.env.*
secrets*
ota_signing_key*

# OBD scan outputs — contain VINs + live vehicle data; keep them local
census.json
sweep*.json
drive.csv
*_drive.csv
# `obd_scan correlate` writes these by default, and report.md's subtitle embeds
# the SOURCE CSV FILENAME verbatim -- which is how a VIN reaches a filename in
# the first place. Ignored for the same reason as the raw artifacts above.
report.md
report.pdf
*_focus.json
*_drive*.csv
bmw_*.csv
audi_*.csv

# ─── Never committed ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ONE place for anything local: scratch files, notes, generated reports, agent
# output, half-finished experiments. If you are unsure whether something belongs
# in the repo, put it here — this whole directory is ignored, so no filename
# needs its own rule and nothing can slip through by being named something new.
.private/

# Tool-created workspaces. These live at fixed paths because the tooling that
# writes them recreates them there; they are ignored in place rather than moved
# into .private/, which would just leave them un-ignored on the next run.
.superpowers/
docs/superpowers/

# Backstop only. These documents live OUTSIDE this repository on purpose
# (~/claude_code/gmc_1500/docs/) — each enumerates OPEN security findings, and
# publishing a findings list to a public repo is itself a disclosure. Keeping
# them out of the tree is the real control; these patterns just refuse a stray
# copy. Every pattern requires a hyphen after the prefix, so the repo's own
# tracked SECURITY.md is deliberately NOT matched.
OBD-BACKLOG.*
SECURITY-AUDIT-*
SECURITY-REVIEW-*
FINDINGS-*

# HIL rig run artifacts (captured serial logs, per-run)
tools/hil/runs/
